+## M4 Android 17 / G965F VaultKeeper backend
+
+The BZI6 Bluetooth JNI's VaultKeeper selector is adapted only for the pinned
+M4/G965F profile. The runtime stack repeatedly waited for
+`vendor.samsung.hardware.security.vaultkeeper.ISehVaultKeeper/default`, while
+the Exynos9810 Hybrid Vendor has no matching AIDL provider. The scoped branch
+patch routes the existing local and bonded key readers and writers through the
+donor's native Bluetooth config backend. It does not install donor VaultKeeper
+hardware blobs or add a broad SELinux allow rule.
+
+The store preflight is metadata-only. Empty storage or exact 16-byte native
+entries are eligible; 32-byte, truncated or malformed entries and a present
+AIDL provider fail closed. Never print/copy key contents. Synthetic metadata,
+donor hash, unique branch address, idempotence and wrong-preimage checks run
+with `python3 unica/patches/bluetooth/a376b_android17_native_backend.py fixture`.
+The compiled image gate also checks the pinned BZI6 JNI Build ID, final file
+hash and ext4 UID/GID/mode/SELinux label. A runtime pass still requires adapter
+ON before timeout, repeated toggles, persistence across restart, and peer
+scan/pair/reconnect/audio tests. G965N and other Android releases are outside
+this patch's scope.
+
+## M4 BZI6 DBFW+ command skip
+
+Fresh G965F attempt0222 logs repeatedly recorded
+`Timed out waiting for Unknown OpCode(0xfdf1)` and Bluetooth service restarts.
+The same build log states that the Android16 DBFW+ capability/call-site
+signatures did not match BZI6. Disassembly of the exact BZI6 JNI Build ID pins
+one remaining optional HCI enqueue in
+`BtifAvStateMachine::StateOpened::OnEnter()` at VA `0x6979e8`. The M4/G965F
+profile uses `a376b_android17_fdf1_skip.py` to replace only that `BL` with an
+AArch64 NOP. It does not return a fabricated controller response, touch any
+other HCI call or disable standard OPP/pairing/audio operations. Donor hash,
+Build ID, context hash, call address and expected final JNI hash are locked;
+the final image gate rechecks them. Run its synthetic and wrong-scope fixtures
+before building. This patch has not yet been validated by a new phone boot.
